  "body": "## What is wrong\n\nThe heavy-lane test `the_users_whole_model_bore_roughs_adaptive_on_each_level` asserts that no D-plate level falls back to the Offset rings.\nThe readings in PR #2035 say that the ring level still falls back.\nThe debug twin of the test is ignored as red.\nThe ignore reason of the heavy test names a normal heavy lane. It does not say that the test waits for #1950.\nThus the release gate of the next cut can be red for a known cause.\n\n## Where\n\n- `crates/app/tests/pocket3d_hsm.rs:152`\n\n## Source\n\nThe read-only Opus review of the merged PR #2035 found this defect:\nhttps://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/2035#issuecomment-6972199583\n\nThe review read the diff only. It did not build and it ran no test. No run confirmed the red result.\n\n## Done when\n\n- A release-lane run of the test shows if it is red.\n- If it is red, its ignore reason names #1950 as the cause, and the test keeps its golden asserts.\n- The `#[test]` count does not change.\n\nRelated: #1950 (open, `blocked`).\n",
